cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WorldSense in your research or project, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "WorldSense: A Reality-Check Layer for AI Agents"
abstract: >
  WorldSense is an open source Python library and MCP server that adds a practical
  judgment layer to LLMs, chatbots, and AI agents. It detects hidden risks, missing
  context, irreversible actions, and real-world consequences before the AI answers or
  acts — returning a structured JSON analysis with risk level, triggered categories,
  consequence simulation, action gating, and rewrite guidance.
authors:
  - name: "WorldSense contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pikappa13/worldsense"
url: "https://github.com/pikappa13/worldsense"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - LLM safety
  - agent safety
  - guardrails
  - risk detection
  - consequence simulation
  - action gating
  - MCP
  - responsible AI
  - common sense AI
